                <head>No. 253<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Editorial Note</hi></head>
                <p>Chancellor Adenauer visited the United States October 27–November 2, 1954,
                    staying in Washington the first 4 days and in New York, where he received an
                    honorary degree from Columbia University, for the remainder of the trip. In
                    addition to the meetings described in the three memoranda, <hi
                        rendition="#italic">infra</hi>, and <ref target="#d255">Documents 255</ref>
                    and <ref target="#d256">256</ref>, and the signing of a Treaty of Friendship,
                    Commerce, and Navigation on October 29, the Chancellor attended a variety of
                    functions which are outlined in a memorandum by GER/GPA, dated November 10.
                    (033.62A11/11–1054) During the several meetings in Washington, President
                    Eisenhower, Secretary Dulles, and the Chancellor issued various statements
                    concerning the visit. See Department of State <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Bulletin</hi>, November 8, 1954, pages 680–683.</p>
            </div>
